cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these data or scripts, please cite this release and the associated manuscript."
title: "Modular evolutionary constraint and lineage-structured switching-helix variation in DNMT3L"
type: dataset
version: 1.1.1
date-released: 2026-10-25
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ghostneuron/DNMT3L-evolution"
license-url: "https://github.com/Ghostneuron/DNMT3L-evolution/blob/main/LICENSE"
authors:
  - family-names: Lu
    given-names: Jie
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6843-9720"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for a clade-aware analysis of vertebrate DNMT3L
  sequence evolution using orthology checks, independently filtered codon
  alignments, phylogenetic and recombination-partition sensitivities,
  codon-selection models, ancestral-state reconstruction, representative
  genomic-neighborhood checks, and structure-informed residue mapping.
keywords:
  - DNMT3L
  - molecular evolution
  - DNA methylation
  - comparative genomics
  - codon models
  - switching helix
